<TITLE>Fail-safe for Door Glass Position Detection</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>When a malfunction is detected in the Hall IC that detects door glass position, speed and direction, or when there is an error of more than the specified amount between the position the power window motor (with built-in ECU) "learned" as the fully closed position and the actual door glass position, the system shifts to fail mode through self-diagnosis.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1"><TITLE>List of Fail-safes for Door Glass Position Detection</TITLE>
<TGROUP COLS = "3" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_10">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "5%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "19%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "3" COLNAME = "3" COLWIDTH = "74%"/>
<THEAD>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>№</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Item</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "3" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Condition</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</THEAD>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>1</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>Sensor Fail (Pulse Direction Malfunction)</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "3"><LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>When pulses in the direction opposite to the drive direction of the power window motor (with built-in ECU) are detected continuously for more than the specified amount during close/open operation.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>2</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2"><PTXT>Sensor Fail (Pulse Stop Malfunction)</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "3"><LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>When no pulse is detected from the Hall IC for longer than the specified time during close operation.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>3</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Initial Fail</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "3" CONSPIC = "0"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM>
<PTXT>When the door glass position could not be read correctly at a CPU reset.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>When motor lock is detected at a position other than fully open during open operation.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>When the door glass position information exceeds the fully open (fully closed) position information stored in the CPU.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>4</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>LIN Communication Fail</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "3" CONSPIC = "0"><LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM>
<PTXT>When a LIN communication interruption is detected.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>The operation mode in fail mode differs depending on the type of fail-safe.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
